  "accepted_claims": [
    "Single-worker async hits retire nine fewer instructions per operation than original and one fewer than main, for both independent and dependent access.",
    "Single-worker blocking hits retain four extra instructions per operation versus main and match original.",
    "Valid evicted nonblocking misses match original instruction count; the previous extra wrapper overhead is gone.",
    "Across eight measured resident scenarios, candidate/main block-geometric throughput estimates range from -1.48% to +0.68%; no measured mean loss exceeds 3%.",
    "Do not generalize resident results to all cache operations: valid evicted nonblocking misses remain about 40.58% slower than main because this branch verifies allocation membership before BUSY."
  ],
  "material_limits": [
    "Only three block ratios per scenario; four of eight candidate/main resident 95% intervals extend below -3%, including both single-worker async intervals near -6%. This does not establish every loss is below 3%.",
    "All 144 hit samples and all 18 miss samples have thermal-throttle-counter increases during the complete process interval. These include setup/warmup/timing/teardown; they do not locate throttling specifically in the measured phase. No measured samples were excluded.",
    "Eight-worker async independent block0-to-block2 throughput falls 3.73% main, 4.97% original, 4.16% candidate. Blocking 1 dependent rises 3.14%, 2.32%, 3.57% respectively. Balanced ordering limits but cannot eliminate shared machine trends.",
    "Hardware counters are enabled only for one-worker runs; instruction deltas are directly measured there, not at eight workers.",
    "Worker CPU time and hardware cycles are diagnostic; no frequency normalization is justified. Raw hardware/telemetry/results must remain available.",
    "Miss result is a perpetual no-prefetch allocated-evicted rejection path; production uses it mainly for metadata prefetch cursors. Report absolute nanoseconds and required semantics, without claiming the path is performance-neutral versus main."
  ],
  "acceptance_assessment": "Evidence supports removing candidate wrapper overhead and reducing async hit instructions without an apparent >3% mean resident regression in this tested configuration. It does not prove universal <3% regression or thermal stability; miss validation cost remains explicit."
}
